137	<article>
138	<h1>Creating New Blocks</h1>
139	<p class="why">Why this matters: every new hardware device your team tests against needs a block — knowing both creation paths means you can add a block in 5 minutes (JSON) or 45 minutes (Python) depending on how much simulation fidelity you need.</p>
140	
141	<!-- ══ §0 TWO PATHS ══ -->
142	<section id="s0">
143	<h2><span class="sn">§0</span> Two paths to a new block <button class="db" onclick="tick(0,this)">Mark done</button></h2>
144	
145	<p>You already know the fast path from lesson 0006 (JSON spec). Here is where both paths lead and when to choose each:</p>
146	
147	<table>
148	  <tr><th>Capability</th><th>JSON spec (5 min)</th><th>Python class (45 min)</th></tr>
149	  <tr><td>Stateful simulation (remember VOLT, return it on query)</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
150	  <tr><td>Computed/noisy measurements</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
151	  <tr><td>Custom block face (live meter, waveform preview)</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
152	  <tr><td>Right-click shortcuts</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
153	  <tr><td>No Python required</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="no">✗</td></tr>
154	  <tr><td>Works without repo change (user dir)</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="no">✗</td></tr>
155	</table>
156	
157	<p><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> start with a JSON spec to verify that your firmware sends the right command structure. Promote to a Python class when you need the device to remember state and compute realistic responses.</p>
158	
159	<p>A Python block is three files and one registration line:</p>
160	<div class="fmap">
161	<span class="dir">silmulator/</span>
162	├── <span class="dir">devices/</span>
163	│   └── <span class="new">my_device.py</span>        <span class="cm">← Step 1: simulation logic (BaseDevice subclass)</span>
164	└── <span class="dir">gui/blocks/</span>
165	    └── <span class="new">my_block.py</span>         <span class="cm">← Step 2: visual widget (BaseBlock subclass)</span>
166	
167	<span class="dir">silmulator/gui/canvas.py</span>   <span class="cm">← Step 3: import + add to BLOCK_REGISTRY</span>
168	</div>
169	</section>
170	
171	<!-- ══ §1 DEVICE LAYER ══ -->
172	<section id="s1">
173	<h2><span class="sn">§1</span> Step 1 — The device layer <button class="db" onclick="tick(1,this)">Mark done</button></h2>
174	<div class="fp">silmulator/devices/my_device.py  (new file)</div>
175	<div class="fp">Reference: silmulator/devices/power_supply.py</div>
176	
177	<p>The device is pure simulation logic — no Qt, no GUI. It inherits from <code>BaseDevice</code> and must implement two methods: <code>_setup_handlers()</code> and <code>_do_reset()</code>.</p>
178	
179	<pre>
180	<span class="kw">from</span> silmulator.devices.base_device <span class="kw">import</span> BaseDevice, ScpiError, ScpiCommand
181	<span class="kw">from</span> dataclasses <span class="kw">import</span> dataclass
182	
183	<span class="at">@dataclass</span>
184	<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="cls">MyState</span>:                    <span class="cm">← optional: bundle state into a dataclass</span>
185	    voltage: float = <span class="num">0.0</span>
186	    output_on: bool = <span class="op">False</span>
187	
188	<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="cls">MyDevice</span>(<span class="cls">BaseDevice</span>):
189	    MANUFACTURER = <span class="str">"Acme"</span>         <span class="cm">← returned by *IDN? automatically</span>
190	    MODEL        = <span class="str">"AX-1000"</span>
191	    SERIAL       = <span class="str">"SIM000001"</span>
192	    FIRMWARE     = <span class="str">"1.0.0"</span>
193	
194	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
195	        self.state = <span class="cls">MyState</span>()     <span class="cm">← initialise state BEFORE super().__init__()</span>
196	        <span class="kw">super</span>().__init__()           <span class="cm">← calls _setup_handlers() and _setup_common_handlers()</span>
197	
198	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_setup_handlers</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
199	        self.<span class="fn">_register</span>(<span class="str">"VOLT"</span>,  self.<span class="fn">_volt</span>)   <span class="cm">← register command → handler</span>
200	        self.<span class="fn">_register</span>(<span class="str">"OUTP"</span>,  self.<span class="fn">_outp</span>)
201	        self.<span class="fn">_register</span>(<span class="str">"MEAS:VOLT"</span>, self.<span class="fn">_meas_volt</span>)
202	
203	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_volt</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> <span class="cls">str</span>:
204	        <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.is_query:                          <span class="cm">← VOLT? → return set value</span>
205	            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">f</span><span class="str">"{self.state.voltage:.4f}"</span>
206	        <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.params:                            <span class="cm">← VOLT 5.0 → store it</span>
207	            v = <span class="fn">float</span>(cmd.params[<span class="num">0</span>])
208	            <span class="kw">if</span> v < <span class="num">0</span> <span class="kw">or</span> v > <span class="num">32</span>:
209	                <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">222</span>, <span class="str">"Data out of range"</span>)
210	            self.state.voltage = v
211	        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span>                                 <span class="cm">← writes return empty string</span>
212	
213	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_outp</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> <span class="cls">str</span>:
214	        <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.is_query:
215	            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">"1"</span> <span class="kw">if</span> self.state.output_on <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="str">"0"</span>
216	        <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.params:
217	            self.state.output_on = cmd.params[<span class="num">0</span>].upper() <span class="kw">in</span> (<span class="str">"1"</span>, <span class="str">"ON"</span>)
218	        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span>
219	
220	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_meas_volt</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> <span class="cls">str</span>:
221	        <span class="cm">← queries return measured value + noise</span>
222	        measured = self.state.voltage <span class="kw">if</span> self.state.output_on <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="num">0.0</span>
223	        noise = measured * <span class="num">1e-4</span>              <span class="cm">← ≈ 0.01% Gaussian noise</span>
224	        <span class="kw">import</span> random
225	        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">f</span><span class="str">"{measured + random.gauss(0, noise):.6f}"</span>
226	
227	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_do_reset</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
228	        self.state = <span class="cls">MyState</span>()              <span class="cm">← restore factory defaults</span>
229	</pre>
230	
231	<h3>Three rules for handler functions</h3>
232	<ul>
233	  <li><strong>Writes always return <code>""</code></strong> — any other non-empty string would be echoed back to the caller as if it were a query response.</li>
234	  <li><strong>Queries return a string</strong> — even numeric values must be returned as <code>str(value)</code> because <code>BaseDevice.process()</code> joins responses with <code>"\n".join(responses)</code>.</li>
235	  <li><strong>Invalid input raises <code>ScpiError</code></strong> — <code>BaseDevice._dispatch()</code> catches it and pushes the error code into the error queue (reachable via <code>SYSTEM:ERROR?</code>). Don't use regular <code>ValueError</code>.</li>
236	</ul>
237	
238	<h3>Why state must be initialised before super().__init__()</h3>
239	<p><code>super().__init__()</code> calls <code>_setup_handlers()</code>, which registers handler methods that reference <code>self.state</code>. If <code>self.state</code> hasn't been created yet, the first call to any handler will raise <code>AttributeError</code>. Always set instance variables before calling <code>super().__init__()</code>.</p>
240	
241	<h3>_register() and _register_alias()</h3>
242	<p><code>_register(path, fn)</code> stores <code>fn</code> in <code>self._handlers[path.upper()]</code>. SCPI devices typically support short-form and long-form paths for the same command (e.g. <code>VOLT</code> and <code>SOURCE:VOLTAGE:LEVEL:IMMEDIATE:AMPLITUDE</code>). Register each variant:</p>
243	<pre>
244	self.<span class="fn">_register</span>(<span class="str">"VOLT"</span>,                     self.<span class="fn">_volt</span>)
245	self.<span class="fn">_register</span>(<span class="str">"SOURCE:VOLTAGE"</span>,           self.<span class="fn">_volt</span>)  <span class="cm">← same handler</span>
246	self.<span class="fn">_register_alias</span>(<span class="str">"SOUR:VOLT"</span>, <span class="str">"VOLT"</span>)               <span class="cm">← alias to existing</span>
247	</pre>
248	</section>
249	
250	<!-- ══ §2 BLOCK LAYER ══ -->
251	<section id="s2">
252	<h2><span class="sn">§2</span> Step 2 — The block layer <button class="db" onclick="tick(2,this)">Mark done</button></h2>
253	<div class="fp">silmulator/gui/blocks/my_block.py  (new file)</div>
254	<div class="fp">Reference: silmulator/gui/blocks/multimeter_block.py</div>
255	
256	<p>The block is the GUI widget. It inherits from <code>BaseBlock</code> and must implement <code>_setup_ports()</code>. Three optional overrides control appearance and behaviour:</p>
257	
258	<pre>
259	<span class="kw">from</span> PyQt6.QtCore <span class="kw">import</span> QRectF
260	<span class="kw">from</span> PyQt6.QtGui  <span class="kw">import</span> QPainter, QColor, QPen, QBrush, QFont
261	<span class="kw">from</span> PyQt6.QtWidgets <span class="kw">import</span> QMenu
262	<span class="kw">from</span> silmulator.gui.blocks.base_block <span class="kw">import</span> BaseBlock
263	<span class="kw">from</span> silmulator.devices.my_device <span class="kw">import</span> MyDevice
264	
265	
266	<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="cls">MyBlock</span>(<span class="cls">BaseBlock</span>):
267	
268	    BLOCK_WIDTH  = <span class="num">220</span>             <span class="cm">← canvas width in px</span>
269	    BLOCK_HEIGHT = <span class="num">160</span>             <span class="cm">← canvas height in px</span>
270	    HEADER_COLOR = <span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">40</span>, <span class="num">80</span>, <span class="num">140</span>)  <span class="cm">← title bar colour</span>
271	    BODY_COLOR   = <span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">240</span>, <span class="num">245</span>, <span class="num">255</span>)  <span class="cm">← body background</span>
272	
273	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
274	        <span class="kw">super</span>().__init__(<span class="cls">MyDevice</span>(), <span class="str">"My Block"</span>)
275	        <span class="cm">#                  ↑ device    ↑ BLOCK_REGISTRY key / display name</span>
276	
277	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_setup_ports</span>(self) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
278	        self.<span class="fn">add_port</span>(<span class="str">"IN"</span>,  <span class="str">"IN"</span>,  <span class="num">0.0</span>, <span class="num">0.5</span>)  <span class="cm">← id, label, x_frac, y_frac</span>
279	        self.<span class="fn">add_port</span>(<span class="str">"OUT"</span>, <span class="str">"OUT"</span>, <span class="num">1.0</span>, <span class="num">0.5</span>)
280	
281	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_paint_content</span>(self, painter: <span class="cls">QPainter</span>, rect: <span class="cls">QRectF</span>) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
282	        <span class="cm">← called by BaseBlock.paint() after the title bar is drawn</span>
283	        dev = self.device          <span class="cm">← access the device for live readings</span>
284	        painter.<span class="fn">setFont</span>(<span class="cls">QFont</span>(<span class="str">"Consolas"</span>, <span class="num">10</span>))
285	        painter.<span class="fn">setPen</span>(<span class="cls">QPen</span>(<span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">30</span>, <span class="num">30</span>, <span class="num">30</span>)))
286	
287	        <span class="cm"># draw voltage reading below the title bar</span>
288	        y = self.TITLE_HEIGHT + <span class="num">24</span>
289	        volt_str = <span class="fn">f</span><span class="str">"{dev.state.voltage:.4f} V"</span>
290	        painter.<span class="fn">drawText</span>(<span class="fn">int</span>(rect.x() + <span class="num">10</span>), y, volt_str)
291	
292	        <span class="cm"># output indicator dot</span>
293	        color = <span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">0</span>, <span class="num">220</span>, <span class="num">80</span>) <span class="kw">if</span> dev.state.output_on <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">80</span>, <span class="num">80</span>, <span class="num">80</span>)
294	        painter.<span class="fn">setBrush</span>(<span class="cls">QBrush</span>(color))
295	        painter.<span class="fn">setPen</span>(<span class="cls">QPen</span>(<span class="cls">QColor</span>(<span class="num">20</span>, <span class="num">20</span>, <span class="num">20</span>), <span class="num">1</span>))
296	        painter.<span class="fn">drawEllipse</span>(<span class="fn">int</span>(rect.right() - <span class="num">24</span>), y - <span class="num">12</span>, <span class="num">10</span>, <span class="num">10</span>)
297	
298	    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_add_device_menu_actions</span>(self, menu: <span class="cls">QMenu</span>) -> <span class="cls">None</span>:
299	        <span class="cm">← adds entries below the built-in "Send SCPI", "Reset", "View log" items</span>
300	        menu.<span class="fn">addAction</span>(<span class="str">"Set 5V ON"</span>,  <span class="kw">lambda</span>: (
301	            self.<span class="fn">send_command</span>(<span class="str">"VOLT 5.0"</span>), self.<span class="fn">send_command</span>(<span class="str">"OUTP ON"</span>), self.<span class="fn">update</span>()))
302	        menu.<span class="fn">addAction</span>(<span class="str">"Output OFF"</span>, <span class="kw">lambda</span>: (
303	            self.<span class="fn">send_command</span>(<span class="str">"OUTP OFF"</span>), self.<span class="fn">update</span>()))
304	</pre>
305	
306	<h3>Four methods you can override</h3>
307	<div class="steps">
308	  <span class="sn">_setup_ports()</span>
309	  <span class="st"><strong>Required.</strong> Called by <code>BaseBlock.__init__</code>. Use <code>add_port(id, label, x, y)</code> to place connection ports.</span>
310	  <span class="sn">_paint_content()</span>
311	  <span class="st">Optional. Called by <code>BaseBlock.paint()</code> after the title bar is drawn. Use standard <code>QPainter</code> calls to draw meters, indicators, text. Access live device state via <code>self.device</code>.</span>
312	  <span class="sn">_add_device_menu_actions()</span>
313	  <span class="st">Optional. Called by <code>BaseBlock.contextMenuEvent()</code>. Add <code>QAction</code>s for frequently-used command sequences.</span>
314	  <span class="sn">_do_reset()</span>
315	  <span class="st">In the <em>device</em>, not the block. Override to restore device-specific state on <code>*RST</code> or right-click → Reset device.</span>
316	</div>
317	
318	<div class="note"><strong>self.update()</strong> — call this after any command that changes device state that <code>_paint_content</code> reads. It schedules a repaint. Without it, the block face won't refresh until Qt decides to repaint on its own (which may be never for a stationary block).</div>
319	</section>
