321	<!-- ══ §3 REGISTRATION ══ -->
322	<section id="s3">
323	<h2><span class="sn">§3</span> Step 3 — Registration in canvas.py <button class="db" onclick="tick(3,this)">Mark done</button></h2>
324	<div class="fp">silmulator/gui/canvas.py:18–35</div>
325	
326	<p>Two edits to <code>canvas.py</code>:</p>
327	<pre>
328	<span class="cm"># Add the import alongside the other block imports</span>
329	<span class="kw">from</span> silmulator.gui.blocks.my_block <span class="kw">import</span> MyBlock
330	
331	<span class="cm"># Add the entry to BLOCK_REGISTRY</span>
332	BLOCK_REGISTRY = {
333	    <span class="str">"Oscilloscope"</span>:       OscilloscopeBlock,
334	    <span class="str">"Power Supply"</span>:       PowerSupplyBlock,
335	    <span class="str">"Function Generator"</span>: FunctionGeneratorBlock,
336	    <span class="str">"Multimeter"</span>:         MultimeterBlock,
337	    <span class="str">"MSP430"</span>:             MSP430Block,
338	    <span class="str">"Code Input"</span>:         CodeInputBlock,
339	    <span class="str">"My Block"</span>:           MyBlock,      <span class="cm">← ADD THIS LINE</span>
340	}
341	</pre>
342	
343	<p>The key <code>"My Block"</code> must match the second argument passed to <code>super().__init__()</code> in your block's <code>__init__</code>. It is also the string used in <code>to_dict()</code>/<code>from_dict()</code> — a mismatch causes silent wire loss on reload (the exact same bug as the original "Function Gen" vs "Function Generator" issue).</p>
344	
345	<h3>Where it appears after registration</h3>
346	<p>Once the key is in <code>BLOCK_REGISTRY</code>, the block appears automatically in:</p>
347	<ul>
348	  <li><strong>Add menu</strong> (menu bar → Add → My Block) — populated from <code>BLOCK_REGISTRY.keys()</code></li>
349	  <li><strong>SCPI Console target list</strong> — the dropdown shows all blocks currently on canvas</li>
350	  <li><strong>Save/load round-trips</strong> — <code>to_dict()</code>/<code>from_dict()</code> use the registry key</li>
351	</ul>
352	<div class="note">The <code>BlockLibraryPanel</code> (left side panel) has a <em>hardcoded</em> list of descriptions (main_window.py:41–47). A new block will appear in the Add menu but NOT in the library panel unless you also add an entry there. This is a known inconsistency — the panel was written before <code>BLOCK_REGISTRY</code> was made the single source of truth.</div>
353	</section>
