415	<!-- ══ §5 CONTRAST ══ -->
416	<section id="s5">
417	<h2><span class="sn">§5</span> Often confused: device state vs block state <button class="db" onclick="tick(5,this)">Mark done</button></h2>
418	
419	<p><code>BaseBlock</code> and <code>BaseDevice</code> both live on the canvas. What belongs where?</p>
420	
421	<table>
422	  <tr><th>Belongs in…</th><th>Device (BaseDevice subclass)</th><th>Block (BaseBlock subclass)</th></tr>
423	  <tr><td>SCPI command handlers</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="no">✗</td></tr>
424	  <tr><td>Set voltage, output state, calibration data</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="no">✗</td></tr>
425	  <tr><td>Measurement noise computation</td><td class="yes">✓</td><td class="no">✗</td></tr>
426	  <tr><td>Display cache (<code>_last_reading</code>)</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
427	  <tr><td>BLOCK_WIDTH / BLOCK_HEIGHT / colours</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
428	  <tr><td>Right-click menu shortcuts</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
429	  <tr><td>Port layout</td><td class="no">✗</td><td class="yes">✓</td></tr>
430	</table>
431	
432	<p>The dividing line: <strong>the device must work correctly with no Qt installed</strong>. You can unit-test <code>MyDevice</code> with <code>pytest</code> and no GUI. The block is untestable without a <code>QApplication</code>. Keep device logic free of Qt imports.</p>
433	
434	<div class="warn">Putting GUI state (e.g. <code>self._last_reading</code>) in the device, or SCPI state (e.g. <code>self.voltage</code>) in the block, breaks this separation and makes the device ununit-testable. The <code>MultimeterBlock._last_reading</code> is a display cache; the "true" voltage reading lives in <code>Multimeter._injected_values</code> and <code>MeasurementConfig</code>.</div>
435	</section>
