449	  <li data-correct="true" data-why="Correct. super().__init__() calls _setup_handlers(), which registers references to self._volt, self._outp, etc. The methods themselves aren't called yet. But the first time process('VOLT?') runs, _volt() executes and reads self.state — which doesn't exist yet — raising AttributeError.">The constructor completes fine, but the first SCPI dispatch crashes with AttributeError because _volt() tries to read self.state which doesn't exist.</li>
450	  <li data-correct="false" data-why="super().__init__() does not call _do_reset(). _do_reset() is only called by the reset() method, triggered by *RST or right-click → Reset device.">super().__init__() calls _do_reset(), which tries to assign self.state = MyState() — but _do_reset() also reads self.state first, causing AttributeError.</li>
451	  <li data-correct="false" data-why="Python attribute access on self doesn't raise NameError — it raises AttributeError. And the crash happens in _volt(), not in _setup_handlers().">Nothing breaks — Python's __init__ methods can be called in any order, and BaseDevice.__init__() doesn't access any attributes before _setup_handlers() is called.</li>
