461	  <li data-correct="true" data-why="Correct. BaseDevice._dispatch() returns the handler's return value. process() collects non-empty responses into a list and joins them with newlines. 'OK' is non-empty, so it's included in the return string. The caller's firmware receives 'OK' as if it were a query response.">The caller sees <code>"OK"</code> in the response string — process() joins all non-empty handler return values, whether or not the command was a query.</li>
462	  <li data-correct="false" data-why="ScpiError(-113,...) is raised by _dispatch() only when no handler is found for the path. A handler that returns 'OK' is found and called successfully.">ScpiError(-113) is raised because returning a non-empty string from a write handler violates the SCPI protocol contract.</li>
463	  <li data-correct="false" data-why="Python strings are never silently dropped. BaseDevice.process() explicitly checks 'if resp is not None and resp != \"\"' and appends to the response list.">Nothing — Python silently discards the return value of methods called as side effects.</li>
