509	<div class="scenario">
510	  <div class="sc-q">You want to add a Signal Generator block. It needs to remember its current frequency (default 1 kHz) and return it on FREQ? Which file do you create first, what class do you subclass, and what instance variable do you add?</div>
511	  <button class="rev-btn" onclick="rev(this)">Show answer</button>
512	  <div class="sc-ans">First file: silmulator/devices/signal_generator.py — create class SignalGenerator(BaseDevice). Instance variable: self._freq_hz: float = 1000.0 (set BEFORE super().__init__()). Register "FREQ" in _setup_handlers(). Handler: if cmd.is_query → return f"{self._freq_hz:.6f}"; if cmd.params → self._freq_hz = float(cmd.params[0]); return "". Then create the block (silmulator/gui/blocks/signal_generator_block.py) and register in canvas.py. Device first, because it has no GUI dependencies and can be tested standalone.</div>
