515	<div class="scenario">
516	  <div class="sc-q">A colleague adds their <code>TemperatureLogger</code> device. The device class sets <code>self._temps = []</code> after calling <code>super().__init__()</code>. They report that everything works in normal use but <code>*RST</code> crashes the device. Diagnose the bug and give the fix.</div>
517	  <button class="rev-btn" onclick="rev(this)">Show answer</button>
518	  <div class="sc-ans">Bug: _do_reset() is called by BaseDevice.reset() (triggered by *RST). If _do_reset() tries to clear or replace self._temps, it executes successfully the first time — but only because the attribute was set in __init__ before the crash. Wait: actually if self._temps is set AFTER super().__init__(), it never exists when _setup_handlers() or _do_reset() is first called from super().__init__(). The *RST crash occurs because _do_reset() references self._temps but super().__init__() called it before self._temps existed. Fix: move self._temps = [] to BEFORE super().__init__(). Pattern: ALL instance variables must be set before super().__init__() in every BaseDevice subclass.</div>
