444	   {t:'<code>*RST</code> calls <code>_do_reset()</code>. If <code>_do_reset()</code> references <code>self._log</code>, it works once (after __init__ completes) but crashes if <code>*RST</code> arrives before <code>self._log = []</code> is reached — which can happen if <code>super().__init__()</code> itself triggers a reset.',correct:true,why:'Correct. If super().__init__() sends a reset signal, _do_reset() runs DURING __init__() before self._log is assigned (since the assignment comes after super()). Also, if _do_reset() is overridden to reference self._log, any call to reset() before self._log is assigned fails. Rule: all attributes referenced in _do_reset() or handlers must be set before super().'},
